Slicing the method string without checking if strings.Index returned -1 can cause a panic; guard the index or handle the case when there is no '.'.
```suggestion
	index := strings.Index(method, ".")
	if index == -1 {
		return nil, nonRetriableError{errors.New("invalid method format: missing '.' in method string")}
	}
	client := method[:index]
```
